<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36825" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξαπ-αλλάσσω</span></b> , 
			Att.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξάπ-ττω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>set free from, remove from,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινὰ κακῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>IA</u>
					1004
				</span></i>
			; (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑαυτόν</span>)
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc"> ταλαίνης ζόης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Hec.</u>
					1108
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			, <i>get rid of, escape from,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κακῶν ἐξαπαλλαχθείς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					5.4
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄλυπος ἄτης ἐξαπαλλαχθήσεται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>El.</u>
					1002
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν εἰρημένων ἐξαπαλλαγῆναι</span>
			<i>escape from</i> his own words, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				4.28
			</span></i>.</div>
